This notebook records how we work through the Pinnacle season. A judge or teammate should be able to open a page and tell what we did, why we chose it, and what changed afterward. If we cannot retrace a design choice, the page is missing something.

== Page Format
- A *date* and an *EDP stage tag* in the title (Identify, Brainstorm, Select, Build, Test, Repeat). The colored dot in the table of contents points to the same stage, which makes the design path easier to follow.
- Active build, programming, and test logs close with a written-by / witnessed-by signature block. Static pages, including this guide, strategy summaries, and appendices, do not need signatures.
- Every figure and CAD render gets a tagged anchor. The Index of Technical Figures links back to each one.

== Notebook Structure
The notebook has three main sections:
1. *Introduction & Pre-Season Analysis* (current section). This covers the game, rules, strategy, and team structure.
2. *Robot 1, Robot 2, ...* Each robot gets an overview, followed by CAD, build, programming, and test sessions.
3. *Appendices.* Works cited and longer code listings that do not belong in the daily pages.

== Conventions
- Decision matrices score every criterion from 1 to 5 and total the scores on the page. We explain the weights underneath instead of leaving a bare table.
- When a mechanism changes, the old page stays. We do not erase iterations. The failed versions usually explain the next change better than the successful version does.
- Numbers come from measurement or testing, and we label them. Estimates stay marked as estimates.
